<title>USA: Mo. house okays bill to eliminate food sales tax.</title>
<headline>Mo. house okays bill to eliminate food sales tax.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-02-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>- The Missouri House approved a bill Thursday that would eliminate a three percent state sales tax on food.</p>
<p>The measure, which now heads to the Senate, was proposed by Gov. Mel Carnahan in his fiscal 1998 budget as a way to deal with a budget surplus that exceeds tax revenue limits under the Hancock Amendment to the Missouri Constitution.</p>
<p>The elimination of the sales tax would cut $230 million in state revenues.</p>
<p>((--Karen Pierog, 312-408-8647))</p>
</text>
